\label{conj:asym_criterion}
    Let $K \subset \mathbb{R}^3$ be a (not necessarily symmetric) convex body. Suppose a specific combinatorial type of Delone decomposition is generated by primitive lattice polytopes $P_1, \dots, P_k$. For any scaling factor $\lambda > 0$, the following three conditions are mathematically equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(i)] \textbf{Covering Condition:} The configuration $\lambda K + \mathbb{Z}^3$ forms a lattice covering of $\mathbb{R}^3$ realizing this specific combinatorial type of decomposition.
        \item[(ii)] \textbf{Containment Condition:} There exist a unimodular transformation $U \in \mathrm{GL}(3, \mathbb{Z})$ and translation vectors $\vx_1, \dots, \vx_k \in \mathbb{R}^3$ such that:
        $$ U(P_j) + \vx_j \subseteq \lambda K \quad \text{for all } j = 1, \dots, k. $$
        \item[(iii)] \textbf{Intersection Condition:} For each polytope $P_j$, let $\{v_{j,1}, \dots, v_{j,m_j}\}$ denote its vertices. There exists a unimodular transformation $U \in \mathrm{GL}(3, \mathbb{Z})$ such that for all $j = 1, \dots, k$, the simultaneous intersection is non-empty:
        $$ \bigcap_{l=1}^{m_j} \big(\lambda K - U(v_{j,l})\big) \neq \emptyset. $$
    \end{enumerate}

