Assume the Riemann Hypothesis and that the non-trivial zeros $\rho = \tfrac{1}{2} + i \gamma$ of $\zeta(s)$ are simple. Then
\begin{equation*}
\sum_{0 < \gamma \le T} \left| \frac{\zeta(2\rho)}{\zeta'(\rho)} \right|^2 \sim \frac{T}{2\pi}
\end{equation*}
as $T \to \infty$.

Assume the Riemann Hypothesis and that the non-trivial zeros of $\zeta(s)$ are simple. Then
\begin{equation*}
