	large open such that $W^{\Br} \neq \emptyset$.	Then there exists a thin subset $\Omega \subset BG[k]$ such that
	\begin{align*}
	    \frac{1}{|Z(G)^{\Gamma_k}|}&\#\{ \varphi \in BG[k] \setminus \Omega : H(\varphi)  \leq B, \varphi \in W\} \\ 
        &\sim c(k,G,H,W) B^{a(H)} (\log B)^{b(k,H)-1}
	\end{align*}
	where 
	$$
	c(k,G,H,W) 
	 = \frac{a(H)^{b(k,H)-1}\cdot |\Br^{\mathrm{e}}_{\mathcal{M}(H)} BG| \cdot \tau_{H}( W^{\Br})}
	{\#\dual{G}^{\Gamma_k} (b(k,H) - 1)!} \\
 	$$
 	where the Brauer--Manin obstruction is taken with respect to the Brauer group 
 	$\Br^{\mathrm{e}}_{\mathcal{M}(H)} BG$.

