\label{conj: random optimization conjecture}
Let $r \in \mathbb{N}$.  Let $U_1^{(N)}$, \dots, $U_r^{(N)}$ be independent Haar random unitaries.  Let $u_1$, \dots, $u_r$ denote the canonical generators of $L(\mathbb{F}_r)$.  Then for every $s \in \N$ and every self-adjoint $*$-polynomial in $r + s$ variables, we have
\begin{multline} \label{eq: optimization conjecture}
\lim_{N \to \infty} \mathbb{E} \left[ \sup_{V_1,\dots,V_s \in \mathcal{U}(M_N(\mathbb{C}))} \tr_n(p(U_1^{(N)},\dots,U_r^{(N)},V_1,\dots,V_s)) \right] \\ = \sup_{v_1,\dots,v_s \in \mathcal{U}(L(\mathbb{F}_r))} \tau(p(u_1,\dots,u_r,v_1,\dots,v_s)).
\end{multline}
Here note that the candidates $V_j$ in the sup are allowed to depend on $U^{(N)}$.

