     & f_i(z) \coloneqq (z - 1)^{i - 1}                  & \quad & (t + 1 \leq i \leq 2t), \\
     & f_i(z) \coloneqq z^{i - t - 1}(z - 1)^{m - i + t} & \quad & (2t + 1 \leq i \leq 3t)
  \end{alignat*}
  are in general position. That is, any $ m $ polynomials chosen from the above are linearly independent over $ \mathbb{C} $.

