\label{conj:stable-p-family}
Let $R$ be a strongly $F$-regular ring, 
and let $\mf b_\bullet$ be a $p$-family in $R$. Then $\mf b_\bullet$ is \emph{$p$-stable}, i.e., $\pstab{\mf b}_e = \mf b_e$ for all $e$, if and only if there exists some $d$ and some map $\varphi\in \ca C^R_d$ such that $\varphi$ is surjective and for all $e$, we have $\varphi(F_*^d \mf b_{e+d}) \subseteq \mf b_e$.

