\label{conj: NTP2 iff counting types}
	The following are equivalent for a partitioned formula $\varphi(x,y)$:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $\bigwedge_t \varphi$ is $\NTP_2$ for all $t \in \omega$;
		\item $f_{\bigwedge_t \varphi}(k,l)$ is polynomially bounded for all $t \in \omega$.
	\end{enumerate}
	Or at least: $f_{\varphi}(k,l)$ is polynomially bounded for every formula $\varphi(x,y)$ in an $\NTP_2$ theory $T$.

\cite{AdlerBanff}\label{conj: Adler}
	\begin{enumerate}
