\label{conj: numb types NIP}
Let $T$ be a countable theory and $\aleph_0 \leq \kappa \leq \lambda$.
\begin{enumerate}
	\item  If $T$ is NIP, then $f_{T}(\kappa, \lambda) \leq \left( \lambda^{\kappa, \tr} \right)^{\aleph_0}$.
	\item If $T$ is not multi-order, then $f_{T}(\kappa, \lambda) \leq  \lambda^{\kappa, \tr}$.
\end{enumerate}
	(Without loss of generality we may restrict to the case $\lambda^{\kappa} \leq 2^{\kappa}$ --- as for $\lambda^{\kappa} > 2^{\kappa}$ this holds trivially by Proposition \ref{prop:tree exponent lemma}.)

