\label{conj:general-topology}
Let $G$ be a graph, let $\cU = \{U_1, \ldots, U_m\}$ be a partition of $V(G)$, and let $k \ge -1$. Suppose that
\begin{itemize}
	\item[(a)] $\widetilde{H}_k(\colorfulcomplex(\mathcal{I}(G),\cU)) \neq 0$, but $\widetilde{H}_j(\colorfulcomplex(\mathcal{I}(G - U_i),\cU - \{U_i\})) = 0$ for all $U_i \in \cU$ and $-1 \le j \le k$;
	\item[(b)] $G$ is a disjoint union of complete bipartite graphs; and
	\item[(c)] $G$ has exactly $|\cU|+k$ connected components.
